Q: Content Security Policy (CSP) &quot;unsafe-hashes&quot; does not work as expected. Browser expecting different hash A: <p>For the sake of closing this question, here is what I learned:</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Most Linux editors add new line at the end of file, effectively changing the hash</p>
</li>
<li><p>Using CSP requires that there is no JavaScript in the served HTML.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>Regarding #2, this is because each inline JavaScript acts as a piece of code that needs to be hash whitelisted individually, similar to the example from the original post. For example in:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;button onclick=&quot;myFunction()&quot;&gt;&lt;/button&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>myFunction()</code> needs to be hash whitelisted similar to an ordinary JS file. Because of this, working with CSP requires registering handlers in the script files, with <code>addEventListener</code>, using CSS selectors.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;!-- index.html --&gt;
&lt;button class=&quot;myButton&quot;&gt;&lt;button&gt;
</code></pre>
<pre><code>/* site.js */
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
  const myButton = document.querySelector('.myButton');

  if (myButton) {
     myButton.addEventListener('click', myFunction);
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Now, only <code>site.js</code> needs to be hash whitelisted for CSP to allow the button handler to work. The key is to organize HTML to allow the JS to reuse CSS classes.</p>

Q: How can I verify website localization across multiple countries and languages during development? A: <p>Use a test automation tool such as <a href="https://playwright.dev" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Playwright</a> and write your tests so they run with <a href="https://playwright.dev/docs/emulation#locale--timezone" rel="nofollow noreferrer">different locales</a>.</p>
<p>Here is an example from their documentation:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.use({
  locale: 'de-DE',
  timezoneId: 'Europe/Berlin',
});

test('my test for de lang in Berlin timezone', async ({ page }) =&gt; {
  await page.goto('https://www.bing.com');
  // ...
});
</code></pre>
<p>You should be able to achieve similar effects in most test automation tools. For example, there is a <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/46908636/how-to-specify-browser-language-in-puppeteer">question here which covers Puppeteer</a>.</p>

Q: Blazor .NET Server Web App CRUD Tutorial - I get two rows when on submit A: <p>This works now:</p>
<pre><code>@page &quot;/crud&quot;
@using Blazor_CRUD_Model_Popup.Data
@using Blazor_CRUD_Model_Popup.Services
@inherits OwningComponentBase&lt;EmpServices&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Crudoperation&lt;/h3&gt;

@* geetbootstrap.com install bootstrap *@

&lt;button class=&quot;btn-primary&quot; @onclick=&quot;Showpopup&quot;&gt;Add New Record&lt;/button&gt;
@if (popup)
{

    &lt;div class=&quot;modal&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; style=&quot;display:block&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;modal-dialog&quot;&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;modal-content&quot;&gt;
                &lt;div class=&quot;modal-header&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;h5 class=&quot;modal-title&quot;&gt;Employee Table&lt;/h5&gt;
                    &lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; class=&quot;close&quot; data-dismiss=&quot;modal&quot; aria-label=&quot;Close&quot; @onclick=&quot;Closepopup&quot;&gt;
                        &lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&amp;times;&lt;/span&gt;
                    &lt;/button&gt;
                &lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;EditForm Model=&quot;Objinsert&quot; OnValidSubmit=&quot;Insertrec&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;DataAnnotationsValidator /&gt; @* Validator for the form. *@
                        &lt;div class=&quot;modal-body&quot;&gt;
                            &lt;table border=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;tr&gt;
                                    &lt;td&gt;Employee Name&lt;/td&gt;
                                    &lt;td&gt;&lt;input typeof=&quot;text&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter Emplyee Name...&quot; @bind=&quot;Objinsert.EmpName&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
                                &lt;/tr&gt;
                                &lt;tr&gt;
                                    &lt;td&gt;Department&lt;/td&gt;
                                    &lt;td&gt;&lt;input typeof=&quot;text&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter Department Name...&quot; @bind=&quot;Objinsert.Department&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
                                &lt;/tr&gt;
                                &lt;tr&gt;
                                    &lt;td&gt;Sarlary&lt;/td&gt;
                                    &lt;td&gt;&lt;input typeof=&quot;text&quot; placeholder=&quot;Enter Salary...&quot; @bind=&quot;Objinsert.Salary&quot; /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
                                &lt;/tr&gt;
                            &lt;/table&gt;
                        &lt;/div&gt;
                    &lt;div class=&quot;modal-footer&quot;&gt;
                        &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;&gt;Save changes&lt;/button&gt; @* With a Validator. *@
                       @* &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot; @onclick=&quot;Closepopup&quot;&gt;Save changes&lt;/button&gt; *@ @* Without a validator.*@
                    &lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/EditForm&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
}
&lt;table class=&quot;table&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Employee ID&lt;/th&gt; 
&lt;th&gt;Employee Name&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Department&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Salary&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
    @foreach (var item in Displaydata)
    {
        &lt;tr&gt;
             &lt;td&gt;@item.EmpId&lt;/td&gt; 
            &lt;td&gt;@item.EmpName&lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;@item.Department&lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;@item.Salary&lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn-info&quot; @onclick=&quot;(()=&gt;EditRec(item))&quot;&gt;Edit&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
            &lt;td&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn-danger&quot; @onclick=&quot;(() =&gt; DeleteEmprec(item))&quot;&gt;Delete&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
        &lt;/tr&gt;
    }
&lt;/table&gt;
@code {
    List&lt;EmpClass&gt; Displaydata;

    EmpClass Objinsert = new EmpClass();

    bool popup = false;

    void Showpopup()
    {

        //code to show popup and clear the boxes. 
        popup = true;
        Objinsert.EmpName = &quot;&quot;;
        Objinsert.Department = &quot;&quot;;
        Objinsert.Salary = 0;

    }
    void Closepopup()
    {
        //code to close popup
        popup = false;
    }
    // Gets the initial table.
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {

        Displaydata = Service.GetEmployees();
        //Displaydata.Clear();
    }

    void Insertrec()
    {
        //code to insert record
        // Displaydata.Clear();
        var ObjUpdate = false;
        if(Objinsert.EmpId &gt; 0)
        {
            // Displaydata.Clear();

            ObjUpdate = Service.UpdateEmp(Objinsert);
            popup = false;
        }
        else
        {
            // Displaydata.Clear();
            Objinsert.EmpId = 0;

            Service.Addemployee(Objinsert);
        }

        Displaydata = Service.GetEmployees();
       // Displaydata.Clear();

    }
    void EditRec(EmpClass ecobj)
    {
        Objinsert = ecobj;
        popup = true;
    }

    void DeleteEmprec(EmpClass ecobj)
    {
        Service.DeleteEmp(ecobj);
        Displaydata.Clear();
        Displaydata = Service.GetEmployees();
    }
}
</code></pre>
